+# Story 8.11: Live Runtime Spine — Daemon Composition Root + Inference Port (keystone) ⚠ kernel
+
+Status: review
+
+<!-- Note: Validation is optional. Run validate-create-story for quality check before dev-story. -->
+
+> **Registered 2026-06-06** (party-mode implementation audit). **Epic 8 Completion Delivery — Phase 2, KEYSTONE.** The first story since 8.4 authorized to break `maos-kernel-core` byte-identity (Charter Amendment 2026-06-06). Closes the "homeless integration layer": a real serving daemon, a reference Spirit reasoning over a **live LLM call**, per-Spirit runtime budget enforcement, and the run-surface seam Story 8.15's journey-acceptance harness drives. **Depends on Story 8.10 (done)** — wires 8.10·AC1's Butler `EpistemicScalarPort` seam to a *production* port and closes 8.10's two carried hand-offs (`None`-footgun + JB-3 production-construction fixture). **UNBLOCKS** Story 8.12 (CLI bridge → J1), 8.13 (live pair → J4), 8.14a (J0 surface), 8.15 (journey harness). Per-journey gate: **J-Butler = 8.10·AC1 + 8.11 + 8.14a + 8.14b · J-Researcher = 8.11 + 8.14a + 8.14c · J1 = 8.11 + 8.12 · J4 = 8.9 + 8.11 + 8.13.**
+>
+> **Recommended dev model:** `claude-opus-4-8` (kernel-touching + composition-root integration; the highest-risk story in Epic 8 per change-proposal §5). Consistent with the 8.9/8.10/8.11 security+kernel recommendation.
+>
+> **⚠ CHARTER-AMENDED KERNEL DELTA — FLAG-Winston.** This story records a **NEW pinned `maos-kernel-core` baseline**, retiring Story 8.4's byte-identical assertion *for this story only*. Keep the kernel delta **minimal and concentrated** (FORK B): the only kernel-core source edit authorized by analysis is the AC3 budget-threading seam (`SpiritManifestBundle` gains a budget field + the scheduler reads it). The `maos run` daemon entrypoint lives in **`maos-bin`** (the binary crate — NOT under the kernel byte-identity rule). The Researcher live-LLM seam is **Spirit-side** (`spirits/researcher`). Measure and record the post-story `maos-kernel-core` line/byte count in Completion Notes as the new baseline; bump the `kloc-check` ceiling for `maos-kernel-core` only if the delta crosses it, and FLAG-Winston in the review.
+>
+> **THREE FORKS — RESOLVED by party-mode 2026-06-08** (Winston 🏗️, Amelia 💻, Murat 🧪, John 📋; **unanimous ratify of all three recommended defaults**, each with binding conditions now folded into the ACs). Criterion = spec-fidelity + long-term-correctness (the trio/criterion that resolved the 8.6/8.7/8.10 forks). **FORK A** (AC4 live-scoring vs Story 8.2 Decision D) → RATIFIED: live recall/faithfulness/hedge are Tier-2/`--live` **reported evidence** only, hermetic CI keeps annotated `expected_*`; traceability + secret-leakage stay **hard-gated on both fixture AND live paths**; + Murat's 4-point assertion contract (AC4). **FORK B** (kernel-delta scope) → SIGNED by Winston with 5 review trip-wires (AC7); daemon in `maos-bin`, kernel-core touched ONLY for the AC3 budget seam (+ a conditional, proven-needed clock trait). **FORK D** (Butler production port) → RATIFIED **boot-loud**, with the load-bearing guardrail (Winston+Amelia): the boot check keys on **manifest posture, not Spirit identity** (a name-keyed check decapitates Researcher / re-ships 8.1 one layer up); + John's negative-boot-test done-bar (AC6). **NEW finding (Murat+Amelia code-verified 2026-06-08, ruling by John):** JB-3 does **not yet exist** (pseudo-code sketch only; `crates/maos-journey-test` is absent; no `maos run butler` construction exists), so the original "frozen constructor call-shape" framing was wrong. CORRECTED: 8.11 **authors JB-3 to the-right-RED** + lands the harness skeleton + named **render-string/scalar-tag constants** (reconcile the `self.belief_variance`→`belief_variance` mismatch); parity is on the **render-string + scalar-tag**, not a constructor signature; **8.11 holds the pen, 8.15 holds the seal** — a non-author reviewer signs revert-to-red at 8.15 (AC5/AC6). Full record: party-mode session 2026-06-08.
+
+## Story
+
+As a director who installed MAOS,
+I want a real `maos run <manifest>` serving loop that loads a Spirit, binds the full substrate, and drives it against a **live LLM provider within enforced per-Spirit budgets**,
+so that the reference Spirits actually reason and run as a product — not only as env-gated smoke arms over deterministic fixtures — and the J-Butler / J-Researcher / J1 / J4 journeys become presentable end-to-end.
+
+## Acceptance Criteria
+
+> Numbered to match the epic AC sketch (`epic-8 §Story 8.11`). **CRITICAL — the epic AC sketch overstates the gap.** Story-creation analysis found that most of the named infrastructure **already exists and works**; each AC below states the *verified current state* and the *actual* delta. Do NOT rebuild what is present. Every code anchor was confirmed in source during analysis.
+
+1. **AC1 — `maos run <manifest>` serving loop (replaces `MAOS_ONE_SHOT` as the production run surface).**
+   - **Verified current state:** `main()` (`crates/maos-bin/src/main.rs:119`) *always* builds the full composition root (substrate wiring at `:119–650`), then dispatches on `std::env::var("MAOS_ONE_SHOT")` (`:663`); each of the ~44 one-shot arms runs and exits. When `MAOS_ONE_SHOT` is **unset**, control falls through to an **already-existing serving loop** (`:3436–3483`) that spawns `IdleWatchdog`, `ScheduleWatchdog`, `ProgressWatchdog`, `SilentFailureDetector` and blocks on `tokio::select!` over SIGINT/SIGTERM/internal-cancel. **The serving loop exists but is Spirit-less** — nothing loads a Spirit before it, so today `maos` (no arg) serves zero Spirits.
+   - **The actual delta:** add real CLI argument parsing for `maos run <manifest-path> [--live] [--once]` that, BEFORE entering the serving loop, (a) loads + admits the named Spirit from its manifest via the existing admission path (the section-by-section `*::from_toml_str` + `security.admit_spirit(...)` recipe at `:3250–3371`), (b) constructs the Spirit object and `scheduler.load(...).await` + `scheduler.start(...).await` it (binding its mailbox via `register_spirit_typed` — **the handle MUST be held, or the mailbox closes with `ChannelClosed`**, the Story 8.4 lesson), (c) binds the Spirit's injected ports (scalar_port/inference/MCP — AC2/AC4/FORK D), then (d) enters the existing watchdog serving loop so `on_idle`/intake fire against real time. `maos run --once` drives a single `on_idle` pass + graceful drain for headless tests (AC5).
+   - **Done bar:** `maos run spirits/butler/manifest.toml` loads Butler, the serving loop drives its real `on_idle`, and (with FORK D wiring) Butler's calendar-conflict scalar **fires its epistemic halt through the production daemon's own wiring** — this is the production firing 8.10·AC1 deliberately did NOT claim. A new `crates/maos-bin/tests/smoke_run_8_11.rs` (or `MAOS_ONE_SHOT=smoke-run-8-11` arm following the existing smoke convention) proves it headlessly with `--once`.
+   - **NOTE on the `MAOS_ONE_SHOT` arms:** "replaces" means `maos run` becomes the *documented production surface*; the 44 existing arms are **kept** (they back the smoke-test suite). Do NOT delete them in this story.
+
+2. **AC2 — A reference Spirit produces a digest from a live LLM call, behind `--live`.**
+   - **Verified current state:** the frozen Inference Port (Story 1b.4, sync per ADR-010) is **fully wired end-to-end already**: `InferencePort` trait at `crates/maos-domain/src/ports/inference.rs:17`; `InferencePortAdapter` at `crates/maos-kernel-core/src/inference/mod.rs:38` (capability-checked, rate-limited, TL-journaled); three **real** provider drivers (`AnthropicProvider`/`OpenAiProvider`/`OllamaProvider` in `crates/maos-providers/`, API-key-gated via `MAOS_ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` etc.); the composition root constructs the `MultiProviderRouter` + `InferencePortAdapter` at `main.rs:587–650`; and `hello-spirit` already calls `inference.complete(...)` (`main.rs:3400`). **Audit claim CONFIRMED: zero *reference* Spirit calls the Inference Port** — Butler, Researcher, Mira, Nash, Observer, Orchestrator all reason in deterministic Rust.
+   - **The actual delta (Researcher recommended):** Researcher's `survey(&[RecalledFrame]) -> SurveyOutput` (`spirits/researcher/src/lib.rs:330`) is pure deterministic compression with **no port field** (`Researcher` struct at `:228` holds only `posture_set`/`pending`/`last_output`). Add an **`Option<Arc<dyn InferencePort>>` seam** to `Researcher` + a `with_inference_port(...)` builder, and a live compression path that, when the port is `Some` and `--live` is set, calls `inference.complete(req)` to produce the digest text (replacing the deterministic `summarize()` at `:622` for the finding-synthesis step ONLY — the walker, citation, and I11 distillate-chain stay byte-for-byte as today). The capability token carrying `Scope::ProviderInfer { provider: "anthropic" }` is issued by the daemon (the `issue_with_mediation` pattern at `main.rs:3376`) and threaded into the `InferenceRequest`.
+   - **`--live` gating (recommended):** a `--live` CLI flag on `maos run`. **Default (no `--live`) = the daemon injects a deterministic replay/stub provider** (reuse `FixtureReplayProvider`, `crates/maos-providers/src/fixture_replay.rs`, behind the existing `fixture_replay` feature) so hermetic tests and the smoke suite stay deterministic and CI-safe. `--live` requires a configured real provider (else fail loud with the existing `InferenceError::Unconfigured`).
+   - **Done bar:** `maos run spirits/researcher/manifest.toml --live` (with `MAOS_ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` set) produces a `SurveyOutput` whose finding text came from a real Anthropic call (provable via `InferenceResponse.provider_attribution` + a TL `Inference` frame), distilled through the unchanged I11 chain (`to_distillation_request` at `:500`, `distill_through` at `:525`). A non-`--live` run produces the deterministic digest unchanged (regression-safe).
+
+3. **AC3 (budget) — thread manifest `time_cap_seconds` into the dispatcher; budget the live reasoning call.**
+   - **Verified current state — the epic sketch is STALE.** `hook_dispatch.rs:87` is **not** a hard-coded literal — it is `pub const DEFAULT_TIME_CAP_SECONDS: u64 = 30`, and `HookDispatcher` **already** holds an injectable `time_cap_seconds` field (`:65`) and **already emits `FrameKind::BudgetWarning` at 80% from production code** (`hook_dispatch.rs:516–539`, via a `tokio::select!` over a `sleep(cap*4/5)` arm) plus `BudgetExceeded` on timeout. The manifest `[budget].time_cap_seconds` field is **parsed and validated** (`crates/maos-manifest/src/manifest.rs:730–781`, `Budget { context_window_size, time_cap_seconds }`, bounded `1..=86_400`) but is **dead config**: `SpiritManifestBundle` (`crates/maos-kernel-core/src/scheduler/control_block.rs:196`) carries **no budget field**, and the dispatcher is always constructed with `DEFAULT_TIME_CAP_SECONDS` (`scheduler_loop.rs:~104`). There is **no separate "reasoning verb"** in the Spirit ABI (`crates/maos-spirit-abi/src/lifecycle.rs:114–216` = 14 lifecycle hooks); reasoning happens *inside* `on_idle`, which is **already wrapped** by the dispatcher timeout.
+   - **The actual delta:** (a) thread the parsed manifest `Budget.time_cap_seconds` from the `maos run` admission path → `SpiritManifestBundle` (add the field) → `HookDispatcher.time_cap_seconds` per loaded Spirit, so each Spirit's `on_idle`/intake honors **its own declared** cap (not the global 30s default); (b) ensure the **AC2 live inference call is inside that budget envelope** — since the `inference.complete` happens inside `on_idle` (already dispatcher-wrapped), confirm the live call respects cancellation and the 80%-warn fires for a slow live call (add a test with an injected slow provider). The "emit BudgetWarning at 80% from production" clause is **already satisfied** — document that, do not re-implement it.
+   - **Done bar:** a Spirit manifest declaring `[budget] time_cap_seconds = N` drives the dispatcher with `N` (test: a manifest with a small cap + a deliberately-slow injected hook → `BudgetWarning` at `0.8·N`, `BudgetExceeded` at `N`); the global default is untouched for Spirits that omit `[budget]`.
+
+4. **AC4 (5-metric real) — score Researcher's ACTUAL live digest. ⚠ FORK A — collides with Story 8.2 Decision D.**
+   - **Verified current state:** the NFR-Aud-7 gate (`crates/maos-eval/tests/distillate_five_metrics_floor.rs`) **deliberately** reads corpus-annotated `expected_recall`/`expected_faithfulness`/`expected_hedge_preservation` (`:57,64,71`) — Story 8.2 **Decision D** records that these are noise-limited against held-out replicator/judge LLMs and **CANNOT be recomputed live in CI**. Only **traceability** (structural non-empty `source_log_ref`) and **secret-leakage** (real `CorpusBackedRedactionPolicy::redact`) are measured on real output; Researcher's *own* distillates already clear those two via `spirits/researcher/tests/five_metric_self_verify.rs`. `maos-eval` does **not** depend on `researcher` and the corpus is never regenerated from Researcher.
+   - **The collision:** AC2 makes the digest **non-deterministic** (live LLM). You cannot pin `expected_*` for a live digest in hermetic CI — exactly what Decision D foresaw.
+   - **FORK A — RESOLVED by party-mode 2026-06-08 (RATIFIED, with Murat's 4-point assertion contract + John's honesty teeth).** Scope AC4's "score the actual digest" to the **`--live` / Tier-2 nightly path** (the same boundary Story 8.15·AC3 draws). Hermetic CI keeps Decision D unchanged (corpus-annotated `expected_*`). **The `--live` evidence pass MUST satisfy all four (else it is flake-prone theater — Murat's risk call, highest-risk fork):**
+     1. **Hard-gate the two deterministic properties on the LIVE digest, not just fixture:** traceability=100% (structural non-empty `source_log_ref`) + secret-leakage=0% (real `CorpusBackedRedactionPolicy`). These are properties of the bytes, not the model — a live digest that cites nothing or leaks a token is **fail-closed** regardless of the judge. (Extend `five_metric_self_verify.rs` to run over the live digest.)
+     2. **The three soft metrics (recall/faithfulness/hedge) are REPORTED with sampling discipline visible:** N (sample count), seed/run-id, judge model id+version, and a **delta-vs-annotated-baseline** (Winston: "live 0.71 vs annotated 0.78, within band" — never a naked score). Pin the tolerance band from the Story 8.2 corpus variance, not from vibes.
+     3. **Direction-only alarm, never a value floor:** alarm (investigate-flag on the nightly + loud fail on the self-trial/smoke, NOT a CI-blocking RED) when a soft metric regresses **more than the corpus noise band** below the annotated baseline. This is John's "obviously-broken floor" — recall collapsing to ~0 is a broken pipe, not noise.
+     4. **Provider-independence proof:** the point-1 hard-gates run against **both** the default `FixtureReplayProvider` path and the `--live` path and pass **identically** (traceability/leakage are provider-independent by construction). If they diverge, the seam is wrong — find out here, cheaply, not in JB-3.
+   - **`--live` polarity is a TRAP (Amelia):** wire it so **flag ABSENT (hermetic CI default) → `FixtureReplayProvider`** (zero network calls, token-free, deterministic) and **flag PRESENT (`--live`) → real Anthropic/OpenAI/Ollama driver**. Pin the polarity in a test (`ci_default_injects_fixture_replay_not_live` asserting zero network calls), not in prose.
+   - **Avoid vacuous-green (Amelia):** the point-1 fixture corpus MUST exercise a real cite-resolution path + ≥1 planted 32-hex secret, or the hermetic hard-gate passes vacuously and only bites on `--live`. Add `digest_secret_leakage_hard_gate_fires_on_fixture` (planted token → gate non-zero) to prove the gate inspects content in the deterministic path.
+   - **Named reader (John):** the Tier-2 live score report is a **release-gate checklist item** read by a named owner before Epic 8 Completion is called done. Reported-evidence with no consumer is a log nobody reads.
+   - **Do NOT** convert the hermetic CI gate to score live output — that reopens the §A2-class flake debt Decision D avoided.
+
+5. **AC5 — run-surface seam + harness skeleton + JB-3 authored-to-RED (8.11 holds the pen; 8.15 holds the seal). ⚠ scope corrected by code-verification 2026-06-08.**
+   - **Verified current state (Amelia+Murat, reading source):** the ATDD checklist (`atdd-checklist-8-14b-j-butler-acceptance.md:213-232`) carries JB-3 only as a **pseudo-code Rust sketch in a Markdown fence**, `#[ignore]`'d, referencing types that don't exist (`JourneyWorld`/`Pty`/`ReplayProvider::queue_scalar`/`world_llm`). **`crates/maos-journey-test` does NOT exist on disk.** There is **no `maos run butler` construction** (`main.rs` has zero `Butler::` refs). So JB-3 cannot be "frozen by 8.15 before 8.11 exists" — that ordering is circular (it is how the sketch's `self.belief_variance` vs production `belief_variance` tag mismatch crept in). **John's ruling: 8.11 authors JB-3; authoring ≠ blessing.**
+   - **The actual delta (corrected):** 8.11 makes the `maos run` daemon **drivable headlessly** AND lands the minimum harness surface JB-3 binds to:
+     - (a) **injectable clock** — drive `on_idle`/schedule cadence under `tokio::time` virtual time; check whether `IdleWatchdog`/`ScheduleWatchdog` read wall-clock directly and add a `trait Clock` seam ONLY if a direct read is demonstrated (FORK B / Winston trip-wire #4).
+     - (b) **pluggable Inference provider** — the AC2 `Option<Arc<dyn InferencePort>>` + `--live`/replay switch, exposed as a daemon constructor param.
+     - (c) **pluggable MCP endpoint** — injected where Butler/Researcher read fixture-replay inputs today (`butler/src/lib.rs:76–77`); the seam 8.14b/c real drivers replace.
+     - (d) **`--once`** single-pass headless drive.
+     - (e) **harness skeleton** `crates/maos-journey-test/src/lib.rs` with `todo!()` bodies for `JourneyWorld`/`Pty`/`ReplayProvider`/etc., **enough that JB-3 COMPILES and runs** (the full Tier-1/Tier-2 suites + `vt100` rendering remain Story 8.15's).
+     - (f) **NEW named constants** shared between production and harness: the **scalar tag** (`belief_variance` — reconcile the sketch's erroneous `self.belief_variance`) and the **rendered halt screen-string** (e.g. `"halted on belief_variance"`). JB-3 references these CONSTANTS, not string literals, so any drift is a **compile error**, not a silent body edit (Murat).
+   - **8.11 authors JB-3 to "the-right-RED" (John's four-part done-bar):** JB-3 ships **RED past compile, at exactly one assertion line (the halt screen-string), for the one reason** — never `#[ignore]`. (i) it **compiles and the harness runs** (RED-because-won't-compile is a disqualifier, not the bar); (ii) everything upstream of the halt-screen assertion is GREEN (PTY spawns `maos run butler --live --replay-llm`, cassette scalar plays, harness reaches the assert and finds the halt string absent); (iii) 8.11 demonstrates with a **throwaway stub** that hard-coding the expected render-string into the daemon flips JB-3 GREEN and removing it returns RED (proves single-assertion redness), then **deletes the stub** so JB-3 ships RED; (iv) **no tag mismatch** — JB-3 uses the (f) constants.
+   - **8.11 does NOT bless JB-3 (the seal is 8.15's).** 8.11 may write the test and may even make it pass via the real wiring — but **8.11 is forbidden from certifying that JB-3's redness was load-bearing** (that is the 8.1 self-certification trap: the author of the wiring blessing that its absence is detected). The certifying **revert-to-red is signed at Story 8.15 by a named reviewer who did NOT write the 8.11 daemon wiring**: remove the Butler halt wiring → JB-3 RED at the halt-screen assert → restore → GREEN. That signature is 8.15's done-bar, mirroring 8.10's proven revert at `spirits/butler/src/lib.rs:297-314`.
+
+6. **AC6 — Close the 8.10 carried hand-offs (`None`-footgun + JB-3 production fixture). ⚠ FORK D.**
+   - **`None`-footgun (FORK D — RESOLVED party-mode 2026-06-08: boot-loud).** 8.10 left Butler's `scalar_port: Option<Arc<dyn EpistemicScalarPort>>` (`spirits/butler/src/lib.rs`) and the AC3 digest pid-resolver as `|_| Some(0)` — `None`/`Some(0)` is the original 8.1 bug as a *legal green path* (John: the 8.1 sin was that "forgot to wire it" produced **no signal** — silence passed). The daemon must make "forgot to wire it" **un-green**: when `maos run` loads a Spirit whose manifest declares an epistemic-halt posture (Butler), it **constructs the production `EpistemicScalarPort` and fails boot LOUDLY** if it cannot (rather than silently running with `None`). Boot-loud chosen over non-`Option` (which churns Butler's test constructors — a wide mechanical diff that hides defects in a story already breaking kernel byte-identity, Winston) — keep the `Option` type for the test seam.
+   - **⚠ LOAD-BEARING GUARDRAIL (Winston + Amelia — the boot check keys on POSTURE, not Spirit identity).** The boot-loud predicate MUST be generic over the manifest posture field: `manifest.posture ⇒ requires_epistemic_halt_port && port.is_none() → FATAL boot`. A name-keyed check (`if spirit_id == "butler" { require_port }`) is **rejected** — it (a) **decapitates Researcher** (8.2: pure-deterministic, NO port, NOT halt-posture → a naive "no port → fatal" kills its boot) and (b) re-ships the 8.1 bug one layer up the moment the next epistemic-halt Spirit ships without its name hard-coded. Enforce the **posture→required-port binding** where downgrading a Spirit's posture out of the halt-set **trips a gate, not a code review** (John).
+   - **Production `EpistemicScalarPort` adapter.** 8.10's orchestrator-backed adapter is a **dev-dep test newtype**. 8.11 provides a **production** adapter — a local newtype in `maos-bin` wrapping the **real `WorkingMemoryOrchestrator`** that `main()` already constructs (`main.rs:223–228`); `process_scalar_write` is `&self` (no `Mutex`). Zero halt logic of its own — the halt DECISION stays in kernel code; only the injection is daemon-side. (Orphan rule OK: maos-bin may `impl EpistemicScalarPort for ButlerOrchestratorAdapter`.) Thread a **real pid** (not `Some(0)`) into both the Butler port and the AC3 digest-provider resolver (`main.rs:284–297`, `memory_backed_digest_provider`) from the daemon's actual loaded-Spirit pid.
+   - **Negative-boot-test done-bar (John — the test IS the done-bar, not the loader code).** Because 8.1's review *marked a fix applied that wasn't*, "boot-loud is implemented" is not an acceptable claim — only a failing test is. NEW paired test `crates/maos-bin/tests/maos_run_boot_loud_8_11.rs`: (a) `halt_posture_spirit_without_port_fatally_fails_boot` — `maos run <butler-manifest, port stripped>` returns a fatal `Err` (specific code, **not a panic**), serving loop (`main.rs:3436`) **never reached**; goes RED if anyone re-adds a `None`/store-only escape; (b) `deterministic_posture_spirit_without_port_boots_clean` — a Researcher-shaped port-less manifest boots **SUCCESSFULLY** (this is the guard that protects against the over-fire predicate decapitating Researcher — **write it red FIRST**, Amelia).
+   - **JB-3 — RENDER-STRING + SCALAR-TAG PARITY (corrected 2026-06-08; the constructor-call-shape framing was wrong — JB-3 binds via a PTY command string + cassette, not a Rust constructor).** JB-3 must ride the **daemon's own production wiring** (NOT 8.10's `with_scalar_port` test injection), never `#[ignore]`. Its frozen surface is the PTY command `"maos run butler --live --replay-llm"`, the cassette **scalar tag**, and the asserted **halt screen-string** — so the parity 8.11 must guarantee is on those two **named constants** (AC5 (f)), shared between production and harness, so drift is a compile error not a body edit. **Authoring is split (John's pen/seal ruling):** 8.11 **authors JB-3 to the-right-RED** (AC5 four-part done-bar) and lands the harness skeleton + constants; 8.11 may flip it green via real wiring as TDD **but does NOT certify its redness was load-bearing**. The **revert-to-red is signed at Story 8.15 by a non-author reviewer** (the only signature that certifies JB-3 is a real guard). Document in Completion Notes: the production entrypoint + constants JB-3 binds to, and the throwaway stub-flip demo proving single-assertion redness.
